.TH GITEA-DEL-USER.SH 1 "2026-04-28" "GitMirror" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gitea-del-user.sh \- delete a user account or organisation on a Gitea instance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bash gitea-del-user.sh
.I name
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gitea-del-user.sh
removes a Gitea owner by name. It checks whether the name belongs to an organisation or a user account, then issues the matching delete API call.
.PP
If deletion is blocked because repositories still exist under that owner, the script exits with an error message indicating manual intervention is required to remove repositories before deleting the owner.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I name
Username or organisation name to delete.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.B GITEA_URL
Base URL of the Gitea instance.
.TP
.B GITEA_TOKEN
Gitea API token. Deleting users requires an admin-level token.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success. Returns 1 on API errors (including owner not found and repo-blocked deletion). Returns 2 for invalid usage, missing prerequisites, or missing configuration.
.SH EXAMPLES
Delete a user:
.PP
.B bash gitea-del-user.sh alice
.PP
Delete an organisation:
.PP
.B bash gitea-del-user.sh my-org
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gitea-create-owner.sh (1),
.BR gitea-sync-all.sh (1)
